1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,069
He built a trap like the fish owed rent.

2
00:00:04,169 --> 00:00:08,239
Out come the pliers, because apparently wood needs suspension.

3
00:00:08,339 --> 00:00:12,408
Now he's tuning the hardware like this thing needs alignment.

4
00:00:12,508 --> 00:00:16,578
Spring by spring, this project is getting suspiciously serious.

5
00:00:16,678 --> 00:00:20,747
Rock test passed. The springs clearly came ready to work.

6
00:00:20,847 --> 00:00:24,916
A little water, one adjustment, and we're still trusting him.

7
00:00:25,016 --> 00:00:29,086
Trap assembled, and off he goes like this was normal.

8
00:00:29,186 --> 00:00:33,255
Now he's in the stream carrying his homemade masterpiece.

9
00:00:33,355 --> 00:00:37,424
First lift, and suddenly everybody wants to know what's inside.

10
00:00:37,524 --> 00:00:41,594
He grabs a rock while the setup waits underwater.

11
00:00:41,694 --> 00:00:45,763
Back into the murky water, because dry land was too easy.

12
00:00:45,863 --> 00:00:49,933
He checks the submerged gear like he's auditing the river.

13
00:00:50,033 --> 00:00:54,102
Finally, the frame hits land with a few tiny surprises.

14
00:00:54,202 --> 00:00:58,271
Everything goes into the bag. Apparently we're keeping receipts.

15
00:00:58,371 --> 00:01:02,441
Then an excavator shows up, because subtlety has officially ended.

16
00:01:02,541 --> 00:01:06,610
One giant bucket enters the water. Escalation achieved.

17
00:01:06,710 --> 00:01:10,779
He moves along the bank like the river filed paperwork.

18
00:01:10,879 --> 00:01:14,949
Bucket goes down again. Apparently we're fishing industrial-scale now.

19
00:01:15,049 --> 00:01:19,118
Up comes the bucket, bringing half the river with it.

20
00:01:19,218 --> 00:01:23,288
And he keeps going, because one scoop was merely a warm-up.

21
00:01:23,388 --> 00:01:27,457
Down, up, splash. The excavator has found its rhythm.

22
00:01:27,557 --> 00:01:31,626
Then the claw pulls up a net full of chaos.

23
00:01:31,726 --> 00:01:35,796
A stick comes out, and the fish definitely got the memo.

24
00:01:35,896 --> 00:01:39,965
The machine stays busy while the shoreline handles the mess.

25
00:01:40,065 --> 00:01:44,135
Back comes the wooden frame, looking much more useful now.

26
00:01:44,235 --> 00:01:48,304
He crouches beside the fish like this is inspection time.

27
00:01:48,404 --> 00:01:52,473
Back into the mud, where gloves remain purely theoretical.

28
00:01:52,573 --> 00:01:56,643
He reaches deeper, because apparently the trench still has secrets.

29
00:01:56,743 --> 00:02:00,812
Next, the plastic crate gets a very personal redesign.

30
00:02:00,912 --> 00:02:04,981
A few more holes, and suddenly the crate has career options.

31
00:02:05,081 --> 00:02:09,151
More adjustments, because apparently the crate wasn't complicated enough.

32
00:02:09,251 --> 00:02:13,320
Into the river it goes, and naturally he follows.

33
00:02:13,420 --> 00:02:17,490
He plants the crate in the current like it's reserved seating.

34
00:02:17,590 --> 00:02:21,659
Then he lifts it back up, because patience lasts four seconds.

35
00:02:21,759 --> 00:02:25,828
Another object comes out, and the crate keeps earning overtime.

36
00:02:25,928 --> 00:02:29,998
Now there's a fish in hand, so something clearly worked.

37
00:02:30,098 --> 00:02:34,167
Crate recovered, bank reached, operation officially looking successful.

38
00:02:34,267 --> 00:02:38,336
And there it is: fish on fire, mission accomplished.

39
00:02:38,436 --> 00:02:42,506
Dinner cooks while he heads back through the greenery.

40
00:02:42,606 --> 00:02:46,675
Fire checked, trail taken, and apparently we're commuting home.

41
00:02:46,775 --> 00:02:50,845
Grilled fish and lemon hit the board like room service.

42
00:02:50,945 --> 00:02:55,014
Knife down, hands in. Formal dining has been canceled.

43
00:02:55,114 --> 00:02:59,183
Night falls, and the treehouse turns into a tiny resort.

44
00:02:59,283 --> 00:03:03,353
He heads inside and immediately clocks out on the pallet.

45
00:03:03,453 --> 00:03:07,522
Outside, the treehouse is now showing off for the cameras.

46
00:03:07,622 --> 00:03:11,692
One last look, because wilderness living apparently needed curb appeal.
